WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.005
Across the board, G-Delta-UQ improves the
reliability of confidence indicators.

00:00:04.085 --> 00:00:08.091
On the structural distortion benchmark it achieves
substantial reductions in expected

00:00:08.171 --> 00:00:12.176
calibration error even at severe rotations,

00:00:12.256 --> 00:00:16.262
while keeping accuracy close to the vanilla model.

00:00:16.342 --> 00:00:20.347
Under size shift,

00:00:20.427 --> 00:00:24.432
last-layer anchoring lowers calibration error while
maintaining or improving accuracy,

00:00:24.512 --> 00:00:28.518
with the largest gains on the most severe shift.

00:00:28.598 --> 00:00:32.603
Under concept and covariate shifts it delivers
competitive in-distribution and out-of-distribution

00:00:32.683 --> 00:00:36.688
accuracy alongside better calibration than other
single-model methods.

00:00:36.768 --> 00:00:40.774
And when its confidence estimates feed downstream tasks,

00:00:40.854 --> 00:00:44.859
it is among the best single-model estimators for
generalization gap prediction and is

00:00:44.939 --> 00:00:48.945
highly competitive for out-of-distribution detection,

00:00:49.025 --> 00:00:53.030
with the pretrained variant frequently the
strongest under covariate shift.
